> - Open item — monthly apportionment of annual caps. The 790-tax-unit and 1,340-tax-unit caps are stated annually, yet withholding is monthly. Market practice, which Mercans follows, is to apportion them at one twelfth per month — 65.8333 tax units (COP 3,447,955) and 111.6667 tax units (COP 5,848,430) respectively — and to test each month against the apportioned figure. No regulation prescribes the apportionment expressly. Carried in the QA report.
> + Open item — monthly apportionment of annual caps. The 790-tax-unit and 1,340-tax-unit caps are stated annually, yet withholding is monthly. Market practice, which Mercans follows, is to apportion them at one twelfth per month — 65.8333 tax units (COP 3,447,955) and 111.6667 tax units (COP 5,848,430) respectively — and to test each month against the apportioned figure. No regulation prescribes the apportionment expressly. The two figures are therefore an operating convention, not a statutory limit. Tax Code art. 206 num. 10 limits the exemption annually to 790 tax units and Decree 1625 of 2016 art. 1.2.4.1.6 par. 3 states 1,340 tax units annually; if the DIAN accepts an annual or cumulative test, the exempt amount in a high-pay month could exceed the apportioned figure, so the apportionment must be kept as a configurable parameter. Carried in the QA report.
